    T8/E10/S13f/L9a/S18a: List and Map are handles; == compares arrays however held; case _; keywords as method names; located checks
    
    From study 3 (findings 1, 2, 3, 19, 24, 29, 30). A List or Map value is one reference to a private record of all its
    state, so a copy names the same collection; Clone() copies. "==" through an array reference compares the elements it
    names (a null equals only a null) and "is" is identity; an array reference hashes its elements. An Array<T, N>&
    returned as the value is copied out (invalid IR before). Slice, length, 'as' and fixed-storage checks print FILE:LINE,
    built and under -i. "case _" with or without a guard; keywords as method names after a receiver clause and after "."
    before "("; "case P => a, b" says a match gives one value.

